    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7055" root="حتك" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَوْتَكَةٌ</span></b>  The <i>manner of walking of him who is
short;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِتِكَّى</span></b> . (Ibn-'Abbád, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also
sing. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَوَاتِكُ</span>, (Ibn-'Abbád, TA,) which signifies
<i>Ill-fed</i> beasts. (Ibn-'Abbád, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  The same pl.
also signifies <i>Young ostriches:</i> (S, K:) the <i>little
ones of ostriches;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَتَكٌ</span></b> . (Ibn-'Abbád, K.)

